<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-top:6.0pt;mso-para-margin-top:.5gd;tex=
t-indent:
36.0pt;line-height:115%;layout-grid-mode:char;mso-layout-grid-align:none'><=
span
lang=3DEN-US style=3D'mso-fareast-language:ZH-TW'>My background is in Compu=
ter
Engineering, and my research areas include digital signal processing,
multimedia processing, embedded systems, servo control, and, more recently,
artificial intelligence. From 1994 to 2014, I worked for several fabless IC
design companies. During my time there, I led the engineering team to valid=
ate
chips, developed firmware and software for turn-key solutions, and supported
customer customizations. I am familiar with every aspect of embedded system=
s,
from the chip, firmware, system hardware, and software. I experienced sever=
al
startup cycles, both US-based and Taiwan-based. From 2014 to 2018, I was
involved with system-level startups. I co-founded <span class=3DSpellE>Orza=
rd</span>
Technologies and developed IoT solutions, including a bus driver monitoring
system and a keyless Bluetooth door lock.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-top:6.0pt;mso-para-margin-top:.5gd;tex=
t-indent:
36.0pt;line-height:115%;layout-grid-mode:char;mso-layout-grid-align:none'><=
span
lang=3DEN-US style=3D'mso-fareast-language:ZH-TW'>Starting from 2018, I foc=
used on
the AI area. I worked as an AI lecturer, with more than 250 teaching hours.=
 I
joined the AI Research Center at NTU (AINTU) as the CEO in 2019, hoping to
bridge academia and industry. As the CEO of AINTU, leveraging my past indus=
try
experience, I can smoothly communicate with all stakeholders, including the
government (mainly NSTC), universities, research faculties, and industry
partners. I have successfully supported more than 32 research teams in
conducting AI research; I have successfully engaged with Google and held a
series of joint AI Bootcamps for seven consecutive years; I have successful=
ly
enabled Google’s research sponsorships for NTU’s faculties, averaging 6=
-8
projects per year; I have successfully organized several large-scale academ=
ic
events in Taiwan, such as MLSS 2021 and the top-tier international conferen=
ce
ACM SIGIR 2023. I have successfully secured research funding from NSTC with=
 4
proposals, amounting to approximately NTD$48 million per year on average. I=
 led
a large-scale research project called “Smart Emergency Department,” whe=
re we
successfully developed 13 AI models and conducted three-month clinical tria=
ls
at NTU Hospital in 2022.<o:p></o:p></span></p>

<p class=3DMsoNormal style=3D'margin-top:6.0pt;mso-para-margin-top:.5gd;tex=
t-indent:
36.0pt;line-height:115%;layout-grid-mode:char;mso-layout-grid-align:none'><=
span
lang=3DEN-US style=3D'mso-fareast-language:ZH-TW'>In summary, I have a stro=
ng and
wide range of technical backgrounds in embedded systems; I have team manage=
ment
and project management experience; I have a strong collaborative relationsh=
ip
with academic researchers in the AI area; I also have hands-on experience in
leveraging AI technology for transforming healthcare applications. <a
name=3D"_Hlk195006591">I am interested in exploring challenging opportuniti=
es.</a><o:p></o:p></span></p>

